  "summary": "Bullseye adds Music alongside its existing Film platform: Billboard 200 rank-bin and same-week head-to-head markets, plain-English question compilation, archived complete-chart evidence, simulated StudioNet GEN pools, and a combined free-points season. Validators judge album identity and ambiguity; deterministic code handles extraction, winners, native payouts and scores. Film oracle and funded pools are preserved. Historical examples disclose known outcomes and use exhibition standings. This draft is not submitted automatically.",
  "judgmentPoints": "One narrow model call compiles the exact album, primary/collaborative artist, named deluxe aliases and Saturday chart date. Ambiguous questions are rejected. A second narrow judgment identifies the debut row from code-extracted archived chart data. Independent validators must agree on complete rows digest, matched positions and the leader quote in their own extraction. CDX capture selection, full 200-row validation, quote checks, winner selection, GEN distribution and season scoring run in code.",
